# APEX dm block device labels (target/a52sxq/patches/apex_dm_relabel). init.rc's post-fs-data has already waited for
# apexd.status=activated when this action runs; it must finish before zygote-start, when system_server scans APEXes.
on post-fs-data
    exec u:r:k4apexdm:s0 root root -- /system/bin/sh /system/bin/k4-apex-dm-relabel

# Same check again for an "add" uevent that ueventd handled after the run above (the 5.4 race can relabel late).
# apexd.status=ready is already set when the run above happens (init.rc's own post-fs-data runs exec_start
# apexd-snapshotde first), so this property event is queued behind what late-init already queued: the second pass
# runs around zygote-start, in parallel with system_server - not guaranteed before PackageManager's APEX scan (only the
# blocking post-fs-data exec is). The third pass runs after boot completes and only helps later readers. Background
# (init does not wait), same domain; the script is idempotent and only logs when it changed something.
on property:apexd.status=ready
    exec_background u:r:k4apexdm:s0 root root -- /system/bin/sh /system/bin/k4-apex-dm-relabel apexd-ready

on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    exec_background u:r:k4apexdm:s0 root root -- /system/bin/sh /system/bin/k4-apex-dm-relabel boot-completed
